{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/602443-sacred-hunt-complications","id":602443,"title":"Sacred Hunt Complications","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-24T19:21:43-07:00","id":602443,"title":"Sacred Hunt Complications","content":"Scenario 1<br /> <br /> A pack is on the hunt, and has a single, defined target. A person, possessed or otherwise easily singled out.<br /> <br /> And someone/something else kills it before the pack reaches it.<br /> <br /> Now what?<br /> <br /> Does the pack &quot;know&quot; this has happened? Do they find any info out, or just &quot;something happened, the hunt ended prematurely&quot; ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Scenario 2<br /> <br /> A pack is on the hunt, but has no desire for it to end in murder. They just want to find a target to get some answers.<br /> <br /> The book really only talks about hunting spirits and how the hunt ends in those cases. It seems assumed that all other hunts are to kill the target. What's the best way to handle a non-lethal Sacred Hunt? If they call this hunt, and simply call up the target for a meeting in a bar, is that a successful hunt then? That feels anti-climatic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scenario 3<br /> <br /> An ambitious pack decides to hunt a large, symbolic or generic target: for example, an Iron Master pack hunting &quot;The Mafia&quot; or &quot;Vampires&quot;, or a multinational corporation (to use an old favorite, Pentex).<br /> <br /> How have people handled this? And what is considered &quot;taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt&quot; when it's something this big and possibly never-ending?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T19:50:50-07:00","id":602471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/602443-sacred-hunt-complications#post602443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scenario 1<br /> <br /> A pack is on the hunt, and has a single, defined target. A person, possessed or otherwise easily singled out.<br /> <br /> And someone/something else kills it before the pack reaches it.<br /> <br /> Now what?<br /> <br /> Does the pack &quot;know&quot; this has happened? Do they find any info out, or just &quot;something happened, the hunt ended prematurely&quot; ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Scenario 2<br /> <br /> A pack is on the hunt, but has no desire for it to end in murder. They just want to find a target to get some answers.<br /> <br /> The book really only talks about hunting spirits and how the hunt ends in those cases. It seems assumed that all other hunts are to kill the target. What's the best way to handle a non-lethal Sacred Hunt? If they call this hunt, and simply call up the target for a meeting in a bar, is that a successful hunt then? That feels anti-climatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>P310, 'Resolution: The prey is brought down (a kill is not necessary) or the pack breaks off the Siskur-Dah by taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.'<br /> <br /> Ideally your werewolves aren't calling a sacred hunt for going over and switching off the lights. Like it explains in the fluff they are predators, and the hunt is a part of their soul, not something easily dismissed. Also it doesn't have to end in death. If the thing is dead at the hand of another, it ends. I'd personally rule that they have to find out it is dead, but the Condition suggests as long as it's dead the hunt is over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scenario 3<br /> <br /> An ambitious pack decides to hunt a large, symbolic or generic target: for example, an Iron Master pack hunting &quot;The Mafia&quot; or &quot;Vampires&quot;, or a multinational corporation (to use an old favorite, Pentex).<br /> <br /> How have people handled this? And what is considered &quot;taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt&quot; when it's something this big and possibly never-ending? </div> </div> </div>The characters in the story throughout the book do something like that. What constitutes a significant action is up to the Storyteller, but we've heard from the writers that it means something actively not involved with promoting the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-24-2015, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T20:44:41-07:00","id":602486,"title":"","content":"As a rule of thumb, a Sacred Hunt is an event with stablished goal, identifiable target and limited context.<br /> <br /> In Scenario 1 they probably have to find out the target is dead, since the Siskur-Dah doesn't grant foreknowledge about its status. It ends when they find the target isn't available anymore.<br /> <br /> In Scenario 2 the hunt ends when the stated intention of the pack is accomplished.<br /> <br /> In Scenario 3 the Hunt just isn't called. Such long term goals are good enough an objective for the Pack, but nonsense for the call of the Siskur-Dah. It probably would, instead, be context for various Siskur-Dah during their lifes.<br /> <br /> The part about it ending with significant actions not dedicated to the Hunt is best understood as any action not derived from imediate necessity. That's where Siskur-Dah works the best closed into context. If you want to bring down a corp, or even just the Wall Mart across the street, chasing a suspicious worker for information is probably worth as Siskur-Dah. The entire project, tough, is too broad.<br /> <br /> Putting it other way, significant is any action that mean ANY relevant amount of time of slack toward the completion of the Hunt. You can do things that you NEED to do in order to survive. You can do things that don't take too much time, or during unavoidable pauses, but NOTHING that would stop you from the Hunt for enough time to make any difference, usualy minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:17:30-07:00","id":603058,"title":"","content":"This is how I'd handle stuff:<br /> <br /> Scenario 1) You find evidence that your mark is dead, you give up the hunt, the hunt is ended.<br /> <br /> Scenario 2) Did you get what you wanted? Hunt over.<br /> <br /> Scenario 3) Another pursuit takes you more than 16 hours a day. Ideally? I would make specific hunts. I'm not hunting Pentex, I'm hunting this manager. I'm not hunting Pentex, I'm not hunting this Wound, I'm taking out this Maeltinent, and this bale hound then, and these wounded spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 07-25-2015, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T12:32:14-07:00","id":603129,"title":"","content":"Take life one step at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}